(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[26 1 "// _ssl's SSL objects (queue 209): _SSLSocket over a socket or two MemoryBIOs, SSLSession and MemoryBIO."] [27 1 "//"] [28 1 "// The pipe adapter. Go's tls.Conn wants a net.Conn it may block on; OpenSSL's callers (ssl.py over a"] [29 1 "// non-blocking socket, asyncio's SSLProtocol over MemoryBIOs) want SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ and an operation"] [30 1 "// resumed by the next call. So each SSL object runs its tls.Conn in a goroutine of its own (the engine) over"] [31 1 "// an in-memory transport: the engine's Read takes what the Python side fed it and, when there is nothing,"] [32 1 "// tells the Python side it wants input and waits; its Write appends to the bytes to send. Control alternates"] [33 1 "// strictly (the Python thread waits on the engine's event with the GIL released, the engine waits on the"] [34 1 "// Python side's resume), so the engine touches no Python object and the transport's buffers have one owner at"] [35 1 "// a time. The Python side feeds the engine one TLS record at a time (its header, then its length), never"] [36 1 "// more, so after an unwrap the plain bytes behind close_notify stay in the socket as with OpenSSL. A callback"] [37 1 "// the engine needs (the SNI callback) runs on the Python thread with the GIL. Writes and close_notify, which"] [38 1 "// never wait for input, are made on the Python thread directly once the handshake is done (tls.Conn's write"] [39 1 "// side is independent of its read side)."] [62 1 "// sslEngine is the goroutine side: the tls.Conn and its transport's buffers."] [74 2 "// alert is the description OpenSSL would send, 0 when none: the SNI callback's (its *al; Go's server sends"] [75 2 "// internal_error when GetConfigForClient fails), a failed verification's (ssl_x509err2alert; Go sends"] [76 2 "// bad_certificate). The transport puts it in Go's alert record while that is in the clear: always for the"] [77 2 "// SNI callback (before the server's hello), under TLS 1.2 for a verification."] [104 98 "// a fatal alert in the clear"] [119 1 "// call runs f on the Python thread (from the engine)."] [140 1 "// pySSLSocket is an SSL object (PySSLSocket)."] [144 24 "// nil: over MemoryBIOs"] [148 26 "// a weak reference, as _ssl's (queue 241: a dead owner fails the SNI callback)"] [164 24 "// the incoming record being fed, for the message callback"] [165 24 "// the bytes at the head of the engine's output already traced (a socket's unsent rest)"] [166 24 "// the version the message callback reports: the server hello's, once seen"] [170 22 "// 3.15.2's got_eof_error (gh-148292): an SSLEOFError raised, read, write and do_handshake raise it again"] [173 1 "// eofAgain is 3.15.2's set_eof_error: after an SSLEOFError, read, write and do_handshake raise SSLEOFError again with"] [174 1 "// no library and no reason (queue 263; 3.14.10 has no got_eof_error)."] [186 1 "// sslVerifyError is a certificate verification failure: OpenSSL's code and message."] [194 1 "// ---- the session cache of one connection: the session given, the session received ----"] [209 2 "// the session's id: its state's digest, so a resumed session renewed by the server keeps it (OpenSSL keeps"] [210 2 "// the session id across a resumption)"] [227 1 "// ---- the configuration ----"] [271 1 "// autoChain is OpenSSL's automatic chain (ssl_add_cert_chain without SSL_MODE_NO_AUTO_CHAIN): a certificate"] [272 1 "// loaded without its chain is sent with the chain the context's store builds for it, as far as it goes (the"] [273 1 "// partial chain of a failed X509_verify_cert too), its root included."] [307 1 "// serverConfig is GetConfigForClient: the SNI callback run on the Python thread (it may switch the socket's"] [308 1 "// context), the configuration made of the context then in force, ALPN without a protocol in common answered"] [309 1 "// with none (CPython's callback returns SSL_TLSEXT_ERR_NOACK; Go's server would refuse the handshake)."] [321 19 "// replaced since the handshake looked"] [326 5 "// _servername_callback: the owner died (gh-146080): SSL_AD_INTERNAL_ERROR, the callback not called"] [332 5 "// _servername_callback: PyErr_FormatUnraisable, then SSL_AD_HANDSHAKE_FAILURE"] [338 5 "// an integer is the alert's description; anything else SSL_AD_INTERNAL_ERROR, with the unraisable"] [355 3 "// OP_NO_TICKET stops TLS 1.2's tickets only: OpenSSL's TLS 1.3 server then sends stateful tickets, which a"] [356 3 "// client sees as tickets. Go's switch covers both versions, so it follows the version this hello gets."] [388 1 "// ownerOrSelf is the owner (nil once it died), else the socket itself."] [396 1 "// setOwner keeps o (None: none) by a weak reference, as _ssl's owner setter (PyWeakref_NewRef)."] [410 1 "// verify is _ssl's verification (OpenSSL's X509_verify_cert with the context's store, then X509_check_host when"] [411 1 "// check_hostname): the codes of OpenSSL's x509_vfy.h."] [428 3 "// the alert OpenSSL sends for the code (ssl_x509err2alert): Go sends bad_certificate, which the transport"] [429 3 "// rewrites while the alert is in the clear (TLS 1.2; TLS 1.3's is under the handshake keys)"] [440 62 "// a fallback root's constraint"] [444 5 "// Go refuses SHA-1 (and MD5) signatures; OpenSSL refuses them from security level 1 on (63 bits)"] [480 2 "// the security level's checks of X509_verify_cert (check_key_level, check_auth_level): the leaf's key, then"] [481 2 "// each issuer's key and each signature but the trust anchor's"] [496 30 "// VERIFY_CRL_CHECK_LEAF (and _CHAIN, which checks the leaf too)"] [520 31 "// VERIFY_X509_STRICT: RFC 5280's AKI on a certificate not self-issued"] [539 1 "// sslCheckHost is X509_check_host / X509_check_ip_asc: 0 when the certificate names host, else 62 (or 64 for an"] [540 1 "// address). The subject's common name is looked at only without a DNS name and without"] [541 1 "// HOSTFLAG_NEVER_CHECK_SUBJECT; a wildcard only as the whole leftmost label, over one label, with at least two"] [542 1 "// labels after it."] [578 1 "// sslVerifyAlert is ssl_x509err2alert: the alert for a verification code (certificate_unknown when not listed)."] [582 13 "// unknown_ca"] [584 13 "// bad_certificate"] [586 13 "// certificate_expired"] [588 13 "// certificate_revoked"] [590 13 "// decrypt_error"] [592 13 "// unsupported_certificate"] [594 13 "// internal_error"] [596 12 "// certificate_unknown"] [599 1 "// ---- errors ----"] [601 1 "// sslReasons are OpenSSL's reasons of the alerts a peer sends, by alert number."] [615 1 "// sslGoReasons are OpenSSL's reasons for Go's own handshake errors, by the start of their text."] [630 1 "// sslReasonText is ERR_reason_error_string's form of a reason: lower case, words apart."] [648 1 "// raiseErr is PySSL_SetError for an operation's Go error: the exception CPython's _ssl raises for what OpenSSL"] [649 1 "// would have reported."] [668 20 "// fill_and_set_sslerror's PY_SSL_ERROR_EOF (set under 3.14 too, read only under 3.15)"] [693 1 "// ---- the transport's two ends on the Python side ----"] [710 1 "// need is how much the record being fed still needs: its header's rest, then its body's."] [720 74 "// from a record's start"] [729 16 "// not a TLS record: the engine refuses its header"] [745 1 "// ---- the message callback (_PySSL_msg_callback) ----"] [746 1 "//"] [747 1 "// OpenSSL calls it from its record layer with each record's header and each message in the clear. The port sees"] [748 1 "// the records on the wire, where the transport carries them: each record's header (SSL3_RT_HEADER), and the"] [749 1 "// messages of the records still in the clear (the handshake's messages up to the change of keys, change cipher"] [750 1 "// spec, alerts). A record sent or received under the keys is seen by its header alone: Go's tls.Conn keeps its"] [751 1 "// keys, so TLS 1.2's Finished and TLS 1.3's encrypted handshake (and SSL3_RT_INNER_CONTENT_TYPE) are not reported."] [753 1 "// sslMsgTrace is one direction's state: whether its records are under the keys, a handshake message's bytes so far."] [761 1 "// traceIn reports the incoming record just fed (flush reports the outgoing ones)."] [782 26 "// before the server hello: the highest version the context allows, as OpenSSL's"] [787 21 "// change cipher spec is in the clear (TLS 1.3's too, middlebox compatibility's)"] [788 4 "// SSL3_MT_CHANGE_CIPHER_SPEC; OpenSSL 3.5 reports a received one under TLS 1.3 only (TLS 1.2's"] [789 4 "// record layer consumes it unreported)"] [813 22 "// the server hello names the version"] [820 49 "// the rest of the handshake is under the keys"] [829 1 "// sslHelloVersion is a server hello's version: its supported_versions extension's, else its legacy version."] [881 1 "// takeCbErr is PySSL_ChainExceptions after an operation that succeeded: a callback's exception is raised."] [888 1 "// fill feeds the engine the next bytes of the current record: false when they are not there yet (a"] [889 1 "// non-blocking socket, an empty incoming BIO)."] [947 1 "// flush sends what the engine wrote: into the outgoing BIO, or to the socket (a non-blocking one's rest kept,"] [948 1 "// SSLWantWriteError)."] [1010 1 "// step hands control to the engine, starting op (nil: resuming it), until it waits for input or is done; the"] [1011 1 "// callbacks it asks for run here."] [1032 1 "// drive runs an engine operation (resuming the one in flight first) to its end: OpenSSL's loop of SSL_do_handshake"] [1033 1 "// or SSL_read with the socket's waits; SSLWantReadError when its input is not there yet."] [1098 1 "// ---- the methods ----"] [1112 2 "// close_notify received: SSL_read's zero return is 0 bytes while it is the only shutdown seen"] [1113 2 "// (SSL_RECEIVED_SHUTDOWN), SSLZeroReturnError once this side sent its own"] [1220 27 "// the peer closed the transport: SSL_shutdown's second call gives up"] [1235 1 "// ---- wrap ----"] [1354 1 "// ---- SSLSession ----"] [1365 1 "// ---- MemoryBIO ----"] [1421 41 "// _ssl__SSLSocket_read